  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/ui/src/model_link_watch.rs`: the new function `resolve` joins a relative link path to the folder of the open project file (`state.project_path`). An absolute link stays as it is. A project that is not saved has no folder, so its link stays as it is.\n- The watch reads the digest from the resolved path. It queues the re-import with the resolved path.\n- `linked_name` is now `linked_to`. It finds the linked model by the link text or by the resolved path. It also gives the link text.\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs` (`finish_import`): a re-import of a linked file keeps the link text as it was written. Thus a relative link stays relative after a re-import.\n- The app layer has no function that resolves a link path. The app tests (`example_catalog`, `model_link`) do not run the link watch. Thus the fix is in the UI watch only. The app crate does not change.\n\n## Readings\n\nBefore (origin/main 10a0a39c0, Windows, `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test catalog_render`):\n\n```\ntest catalog_cases_open_and_frame_cleanly ... FAILED\n...\\examples\\catalog\\3d\\rough-finish\\rough-finish.camproj failed to open: rough-finish kept as it is: its linked file model/rough-finish.obj cannot be read (The system cannot find the path specified. (os error 3))\n```\n\nAfter (this branch): `catalog_cases_open_and_frame_cleanly ... ok`, `test result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed; 1 ignored`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `model_link_tests::a_relative_link_resolves_against_the_project_folder`: a link `part.stl` in a temp folder, with the working directory `crates/ui`. The watch gives no link error. A change of the file imports it again, and the link stays `part.stl`.\n- `model_link_tests::an_absolute_link_ignores_the_project_folder_and_an_unsaved_project_keeps_the_path`: an absolute link is read as it is when the project is in a different folder. A relative link of a project that is not saved keeps the old reading and is refused by name.\n- `catalog_render::catalog_cases_open_and_frame_cleanly` (not changed).\n\n## Quick gate (head 64bace673)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test catalog_render`: 2 passed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib model_link`: 5 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI on a desktop. The tests use the headless state only.\n- The real open of a project from disk with a relative link and a file change after the open. The test sets `project_path` directly.\n- The MCP and CLI paths. They do not run the link watch.\n- No heavy lane. This is a P2 UI change.\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs` is already longer than 400 lines. This PR adds 10 lines to `finish_import` and does not split the file.\n\nChangelog: A linked model with a relative path is now read from the folder of the project file, not from the folder the program started in.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3686\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
